1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
You'd think 5,000 metres needs an oxygen mask.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
China's highest railway climbs to 5,072 m.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
Up there, the air holds 40% less oxygen.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
But every carriage is sealed, like a plane.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Past Golmud, it pumps in its own oxygen.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
Double-tap if you'd ride the roof of the world.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
960 km of track runs above 4,000 m.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
No mask needed, just breathe and watch.

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,600
★ Expert Tip: sleep a night in Xining first to acclimatise.

11
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,000
Would you take the world's highest train? Tell me.
